From: Yusuf İhsan KILINÇ <78423442+yusufklncc@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:30:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 10] anv: enable H.264 encode on Xe2

Xe2 (Battlemage, media 13.01) runs the Gfx12.5 H.264 VDEnc path with two
changes taken from Intel's media-driver (Xe2_HPM AVC encoder):

 - VDENC_AVC_IMG_STATE is 26 dwords on Xe_LPM+/Xe2 (20 on DG2): add the Xe2
   layout to xe2.xml and program dwords 1-25 with the Xe2_HPM settings
   (encode_avc_vdenc_const_settings_xe2_hpm_open.h, target usage 4).
 - The collocated MV write buffer, the 8x scaled reference and the backward
   4x DS reference in VDENC_PIPE_BUF_ADDR_STATE apply to Gfx12.5 and later,
   not only to Gfx12.5.

The HuC BRC tables of Xe2_HPM equal Xe_LPM+'s, so the H.264 BRC path is
unchanged; its SLB size follows the longer image state through the genxml
length. Wa_18011246551 is not set on BMG.

Tested on Arc B580: CQP, CBR and VBR (HuC BRC), I/P/B, 720p-4K; output
decodes with libavcodec's software H.264 decoder without errors
(1080p testsrc2 QP 24: 50.4 dB Y; VBR 8 Mbit/s: 47.2 dB, 8.6 Mbit/s).

Applies on top of patches 0001-0008 and the widlarizer Xe2 HEVC VDEnc series
(src/mesa-venc branch xe2-venc).
